s":"Jose Montero","x":"Our total fuel expense for the quarter was $36.7 million above Q4 2017 of which $29 million are related to the fuel price increase and the rest due to the additional capacity flown during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/14/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q4-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2018 Q4","e":"cpa","d":"2018-02-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"However, we continue to deliver industry-leading unit costs, and we continue pursuing our cost-savings initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/14/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q4-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2018 Q4","e":"cpa","d":"2018-02-13","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"So, these are things that we are looking at very closely right now and of course in light of what you mentioned, of what is the impact of the 190 in certain secondary markets where that is the right size of aircraft.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/02/14/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q4-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2018 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2018-11-15","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"Our total fuel expense for the quarter was $57.2 million above Q3 2017, of which $48.6 million are related to the fuel price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/15/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2018 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2018-11-15","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"On the cost side, CASM came in at $0.09, 4.3% higher year-over-year due to higher fuel costs; however, ex-fuel unit costs, came in at $0.06 or 5.5% lower year-over-year due to the timing of certain events and cost reduction efforts.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/15/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2018 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2018-11-15","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"However, we continue to deliver industry leading unit costs and we continue pursuing our cost savings initiatives.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/11/15/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2018-earnings-conference-c.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2019 Q1","e":"cpa","d":"2019-05-09","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"But it is affecting us and we can assume that we would have been raising our guidance if it was not for the MAX grounding.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/05/09/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q1-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2019 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2019-08-08","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"So I have to start by saying that given this MAX situation, we basically fast forward a lot of the cost savings efforts that we had been working on over the last several months.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/08/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2019 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2019-08-08","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"It was really a team effort here in terms of the cost savings that we delivered.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/08/08/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2019 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2019-11-14","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"Despite all of that, based on the strong third quarter results, we are reaffirming our guidance for 2019 and expect to deliver an operating margin of approximately 16% for the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/11/14/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2019-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q1","e":"cpa","d":"2020-05-09","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"We're working on cost reduction initiatives, including renegotiating our remain supplier contract and reevaluating our entire fixed cost structure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/09/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q1","e":"cpa","d":"2020-05-09","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"But then the product will be simplified also, as I mentioned before to reduce the interaction between crews and passengers, and there will be some cost savings there too, which should offset the value of -- the additional cost from bio-safety.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/05/09/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q1-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2020-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Matthew Wisniewski","x":"Or is it not necessarily prudent to take that much cost out of the business given it impairs you going forward?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/07/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2020-08-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Conor Cunningham","x":"I would think that the majority of it's revenue-related, but just curious if -- because it just seems like you have achieved a lot of your cost reduction stuff already?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/08/07/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2020-earnings-call-transcr.aspx"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2020-11-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"…we have adjusted the size of the company to better match our future capacity and continue working on cost reduction efforts, as we believe, keeping a competitive cost structure and a strong financial position will keep us among the best procurements to come out ahead once this crisis is over.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/19/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2020-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"CPA 2020 Q4","e":"cpa","d":"2021-02-11","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Pedro Heilbron","x":"…all capital expenditures that were deemed non-essential and immediately began a series of cost reduction initiatives, including contract renegotiations with suppliers and a thorough evaluation of our entire cost structure; adjusting the company's size to better match future capacity over…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/02/12/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q4-2020-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"CPA 2021 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2021-08-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Stephen Trent","x":"Could you refresh my memory, Panama itself, I know that the Panama has been allowing in transit passengers to pass through your airport with no problems.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"CPA 2021 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2021-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Jose Montero","x":"We continue with our cost savings initiatives, and we are targeting to achieve our unit cost below $0.06 once we reach 100% of our pre-COVID-19 capacity.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"CPA 2021 Q2","e":"cpa","d":"2021-08-05","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Ray Wong","x":"Just like a sense of like when you see network -- when you see other competitors across your network restructuring, etc., going through harsher times.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/05/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q2-2021-earnings-call-transcr/"},{"c":"CPA 2021 Q3","e":"cpa","d":"2021-11-18","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Stephen Trent","x":"When we think about the stickiness on the fare side, especially, let's say on some of your low density routes, is there -- is it fair to say that there's still so much pent-up demand that you are seeing very good fare pass through even on non-business travelers?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/18/copa-holdings-sa-cpa-q3-2021-earning